From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michaela Laurencin <mlaurencin@electronjs.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:48:46 -0400
Subject: fix: avoid updating display affinity for hidden owned windows

Calling SetWindowDisplayAffinity on a hidden owned HWND can cause DWM to materialize its surface while Windows still reports it hidden.
Skip hidden owned windows; DesktopWindowTreeHostWin::Show updates inherited affinity before making each window visible.

This patch is temporary and should be removed once the fix is upstreamed in Chromium.
Verify by checking whether ApplyAffinityToOwnedWindows skips hidden HWNDs.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_window_tree_host_win.cc b/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_window_tree_host_win.cc
--- a/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_window_tree_host_win.cc
+++ b/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_window_tree_host_win.cc
@@ -153,7 +153,12 @@ void ApplyAffinityToOwnedWindows(HWND owner_hwnd, DWORD affinity) {
         constexpr int kMaxOwnerDepth = 32;
         for (int depth = 0; current_owner && depth < kMaxOwnerDepth; ++depth) {
           if (current_owner == enum_data->owner) {
-            ::SetWindowDisplayAffinity(hwnd, enum_data->affinity);
+            // Applying display affinity to a hidden owned window can cause DWM
+            // to materialize its surface. The window will inherit its owner's
+            // affinity when it is shown.
+            if (::IsWindowVisible(hwnd)) {
+              ::SetWindowDisplayAffinity(hwnd, enum_data->affinity);
+            }
             break;
           }
           current_owner = ::GetWindow(current_owner, GW_OWNER);
